---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Section from "../components/Section.astro";
import Eyebrow from "../components/Eyebrow.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Setup 101 · mogkit"
  description="Get mogkit running, even if you've never opened a terminal. From zero to your first skill, step by step."
>
  <article class="container-tight pt-16 sm:pt-20 pb-8">
    <Eyebrow>Setup 101</Eyebrow>
    <h1 class="font-display text-4xl sm:text-5xl text-halo tracking-tightest leading-[0.98] mt-4 lift-in lift-in-2">
      If you've never opened a terminal,<br/>
      <span class="text-mercury">start here.</span>
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-6 text-lg text-chrome leading-relaxed lift-in lift-in-3">
      mogkit runs in your computer's terminal. The terminal is an app where
      you type a command and press Enter, and the computer replies in text.
      Every command you need is on this page, ready to copy. By the end you
      will have run your first PM skill.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4 text-chrome leading-relaxed lift-in lift-in-4">
      Estimated time: <span class="font-mono text-halo">15 minutes</span>,
      most of it waiting for installs. mogkit is free. You need one AI
      assistant to run it: Claude Code, OpenAI's Codex, or Cursor.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4 text-chrome leading-relaxed lift-in lift-in-4">
      Use ChatGPT or another chat app and don't want to install anything?
      Open <a class="text-mercury hover:text-halo underline decoration-graphite underline-offset-4" href="/wedges">any skills page</a>, press
      "Copy for ChatGPT or any AI chat" on a skill, paste it into a new
      chat, then paste your work under it. You can stop reading here.
    </p>
  </article>

  <Section spacing="tight">
    <div class="container-tight">
      <Eyebrow>Step 1</Eyebrow>
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl text-halo tracking-tight mt-3 mb-4">Open the terminal</h2>
      <p class="text-chrome leading-relaxed">Open the app called <strong class="text-halo font-medium">Terminal</strong>:</p>
      <ul class="mt-3 list-disc pl-6 space-y-1.5 text-chrome marker:text-ash">
        <li><strong class="text-halo font-medium">Mac:</strong> press <code>⌘ + Space</code>, type <code>Terminal</code>, hit Enter.</li>
        <li><strong class="text-halo font-medium">Windows:</strong> install <a class="text-mercury hover:text-halo underline decoration-graphite underline-offset-4" href="https://learn.microsoft.com/windows/wsl/install">WSL</a> first (one-time), then open the Ubuntu app.</li>
        <li><strong class="text-halo font-medium">Linux:</strong> open your Terminal app.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="mt-4 text-chrome leading-relaxed">
        You'll see a blinking cursor next to your username. Type or paste a
        command there and press Enter. The computer runs it and prints the
        result. Every step below works this way.
      </p>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section spacing="tight">
    <div class="container-tight">
      <Eyebrow>Step 2</Eyebrow>
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl text-halo tracking-tight mt-3 mb-4">Install Node</h2>
      <p class="text-chrome leading-relaxed">
        Node is a free program that mogkit needs in order to run. Check
        whether you already have it:
      </p>
      <pre class="mt-4"><code>node --version</code></pre>
      <p class="mt-4 text-chrome leading-relaxed">
        If that printed <code>v22</code> or a higher number, you're done with
        this step. If it said "command not found" or showed a lower number,
        install Node:
      </p>
      <ul class="mt-3 list-disc pl-6 space-y-1.5 text-chrome marker:text-ash">
        <li><strong class="text-halo font-medium">Easy:</strong> download the installer marked LTS from <a class="text-mercury hover:text-halo underline decoration-graphite underline-offset-4" href="https://nodejs.org">nodejs.org</a>, open it, and click through. Then close the terminal and open it again.</li>
        <li><strong class="text-halo font-medium">If you already use nvm:</strong> run <code>nvm install --lts</code>.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section spacing="tight">
    <div class="container-tight">
      <Eyebrow>Step 3</Eyebrow>
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl text-halo tracking-tight mt-3 mb-4">Install an AI assistant</h2>
      <p class="text-chrome leading-relaxed">
        The assistant is the AI that reads your work and runs the mogkit
        skills. Pick one. If you already pay for one of these, use that.
      </p>
      <ul class="mt-3 list-disc pl-6 space-y-1.5 text-chrome marker:text-ash">
        <li><strong class="text-halo font-medium">Claude Code</strong>, by Anthropic. Needs a paid Claude plan. Install from <a class="text-mercury hover:text-halo underline decoration-graphite underline-offset-4" href="https://claude.com/claude-code">claude.com/claude-code</a>.</li>
        <li><strong class="text-halo font-medium">Codex</strong>, by OpenAI. Comes with paid ChatGPT plans. Install from <a class="text-mercury hover:text-halo underline decoration-graphite underline-offset-4" href="https://developers.openai.com/codex">developers.openai.com/codex</a>.</li>
        <li><strong class="text-halo font-medium">Cursor</strong>. A desktop app with a free tier. Download from <a class="text-mercury hover:text-halo underline decoration-graphite underline-offset-4" href="https://cursor.com">cursor.com</a>.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="mt-4 text-chrome leading-relaxed">
        Sign in when the assistant asks. mogkit installs its skills for all
        three, so you can switch later without redoing anything.
      </p>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section spacing="tight">
    <div class="container-tight">
      <Eyebrow>Step 4</Eyebrow>
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl text-halo tracking-tight mt-3 mb-4">Install mogkit and create your workspace</h2>
      <p class="text-chrome leading-relaxed">
        Install mogkit. This makes the <code>mogkit</code> command available
        everywhere on your computer:
      </p>
      <pre class="mt-4"><code>npm install -g mogkit</code></pre>
      <p class="mt-4 text-chrome leading-relaxed">
        Then create a workspace. This is one folder that holds your
        research, your notes and the skills. The second line moves you
        into it:
      </p>
      <pre class="mt-4"><code>mogkit init my-workspace
cd my-workspace</code></pre>
      <p class="mt-4 text-chrome leading-relaxed">That's it. You now have a folder with:</p>
      <ul class="mt-3 list-disc pl-6 space-y-1.5 text-chrome marker:text-ash">
        <li><code>CLAUDE.md</code> and <code>AGENTS.md</code>: instructions your assistant reads every time you open this folder</li>
        <li><code>sources/</code>: where your interviews, tickets and research go</li>
        <li><code>graph/</code>: a map of your research, built by the Discovery skills</li>
        <li><code>knowledge/</code>: a saved copy of every review you run</li>
        <li><code>.claude/skills/</code> and <code>.agents/skills/</code>: all 21 mogkit skills, installed for Claude Code, Codex and Cursor</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section spacing="tight">
    <div class="container-tight">
      <Eyebrow>Step 5</Eyebrow>
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl text-halo tracking-tight mt-3 mb-4">Check your setup</h2>
      <p class="text-chrome leading-relaxed">From inside the workspace, run:</p>
      <pre class="mt-4"><code>mogkit doctor</code></pre>
      <p class="mt-4 text-chrome leading-relaxed">
        Every check should pass with a green <code>✓</code>. If one fails,
        the message says what to fix and how.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-chrome leading-relaxed">
        Want sample research to try the Discovery skills on? Load ours:
      </p>
      <pre class="mt-4"><code>mogkit demo</code></pre>
      <p class="mt-4 text-chrome leading-relaxed">
        That copies 8 sample files (interviews, tickets, a PRD, a memo,
        competitor research) into <code>sources/</code>, which is enough for
        every Discovery skill to produce a result on day one.
      </p>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section spacing="tight">
    <div class="container-tight">
      <Eyebrow>Step 6</Eyebrow>
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl text-halo tracking-tight mt-3 mb-4">Run your first skill</h2>
      <p class="text-chrome leading-relaxed">
        Start your assistant from inside your workspace. Type
        <code>claude</code> for Claude Code or <code>codex</code> for Codex.
        For Cursor, open the app, choose File, then Open Folder, and pick
        your workspace folder.
      </p>
      <pre class="mt-4"><code>claude</code></pre>
      <p class="mt-4 text-chrome leading-relaxed">
        Then ask for a skill by name and paste your input under it. A good
        first one is <code>tradeoff-frame</code>. Give it a decision your
        team disagrees on, with two real options. This wording works in all
        three assistants:
      </p>
      <pre class="mt-4"><code>Use the tradeoff-frame skill on this decision:
We are deciding whether to build a Slack integration ourselves
or partner through Zapier. Engineering wants to build. Growth
wants to partner.</code></pre>
      <p class="mt-4 text-chrome leading-relaxed">
        In Claude Code and Cursor you can also type
        <code>/tradeoff-frame</code> as a shortcut.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-chrome leading-relaxed">
        You get back the real points of disagreement, what each option
        gains and gives up, and whether the decision is easy to reverse.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-chrome leading-relaxed">
        It won't pick the answer. That is deliberate. It lays out the
        decision so you can make it well.
      </p>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section hairline>
    <div class="container-tight">
      <Eyebrow>Where to go next</Eyebrow>
      <ul class="mt-4 list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-chrome marker:text-ash">
        <li>
          <a class="text-mercury hover:text-halo underline decoration-graphite underline-offset-4" href="/wedges">Browse the skills by topic</a>. Launching something soon? Start with <a class="text-mercury hover:text-halo underline decoration-graphite underline-offset-4" href="/wedges/gtm">GTM and Launch</a>. Doing customer research? Start with <a class="text-mercury hover:text-halo underline decoration-graphite underline-offset-4" href="/wedges/discovery">Discovery</a>.
        </li>
        <li>
          The <a class="text-mercury hover:text-halo underline decoration-graphite underline-offset-4" href="/workflows">Workflow Library</a> has step-by-step guides for putting AI to work on recurring PM chores.
        </li>
        <li>
          If something stops working, run <code>mogkit doctor</code>. It finds most setup problems and explains the fix in plain language.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </Section>
</BaseLayout>
